# Reference talk

Follow the style of https://github.com/RSamyak/2026-08-bmathreunion-talk (`slides.qmd`, `theme.scss`).  Different talk: copy the style, not the content.

When in doubt, look at that talk and match its layout, structure, and style.

- Title slide: title, then stacked author lines (`name · affiliation`, `venue · date`).
- A visual map of the talk's structure up front; each section opens on a coloured divider that recalls it.
- Content slides: `{.content}` with the body in `::: {.cbody}`; short bullets in `{.incremental}`, sub-bullets for detail.
- The punchline of a slide is a `[...]{.fragment .below-note}` line, revealed last.
- One colour per section; its slides carry a tint and a corner label.
- Close on a takeaway slide: one column per section, then thanks and contact.
- Plain, wry wording.  Maths where it earns its place.
